  "title": "In the Hall of the Mountain King",
  "composer": "Edvard Grieg",
  "about": "Grieg wrote this music for Henrik Ibsen's play Peer Gynt, first staged in Christiania, today's Oslo, in 1876. In this scene, the trolls crowd around Peer in the hall of their king. The same short tune comes back again and again, each time louder and faster, until it crashes to an end.",
  "funFact": "Grieg himself wrote that this piece reeked of cow pies and trollish self-satisfaction, and he could hardly bear to hear it.",
